/gs/main.go, promise.go,\nartifact.go, review_request.go and land.go at 5b54561d, usage.go at ccd161c6,\nwork_next.go at 62905d95, preflight.go at df549e33, internal/workroom/fold.go\nat 762f34ae, internal/app/request_authoring.go at 80d4fbf7 and\ninternal/statusview/query.go at 2348ebe6. The duplicate second cmd/gs/main.go\nentry is gone. The docset gate passes over dead citations either way, so it\ndoes not catch this.\n\n2. Shorter, with the refusal catalogues replaced by links. SKILL.md is 208\nlines and 1439 words against 213 and 1499; AGENTS.md is 40 lines and 275 words\nagainst 100 and 756. The pair an actor reads each cycle went from 2255 words\nto 1714. Every refusal list removed from a step was confirmed present in that\ncommand's reference page at this head: promise.md:63, artifact.md:79,\nreview-request.md:66 and review.md:104 each carry the table, and land.md\nstates the same refusals in its ordered account at lines 83 to 104. No step lost a rule.\nTwo rules were added: check the evidence rather than the claim, and a gate you\ndid not run or did not read is not evidence.\n\n3. The drift is resolved towards SKILL.md. AGENTS.md no longer restates the\nloop, the worktree section, the presence definition or the ephemerality rules.\nIt names three rules this repository deliberately repeats, and says that is\nwhat they are, and keeps what is genuinely local: the superseded-world merge\nrefusal, the dot-artifact migration, and the presence policy.\n\n4. `make docs` and `make test` both green at exactly 3049d18b, exit 0, and\nthe one suite that reads these pages was rerun uncached: docset with -count=1\nat 39.8s. The new main invalidated most of the Go cache, so cmd/gs (459.8s),\ncmd/gitseq-mcp (60.3s), cmd/gitseq-github (16.0s), host (9.9s),\ninternal/workroom (6.9s) and internal/residentclient (0.5s) all ran fresh.\ninternal/app and the other packages report ok from cache, their inputs being\nbyte-identical to the run at a15234fa where internal/app took 228.5